{
  "description": "Keyword mappings for auto-detecting tags from transcripts. Keywords are case-insensitive. Every key MUST be a live tag in tags.json — sync-vlogs.js writes these straight into post frontmatter, so a key that isn't in the registry re-creates a retired tag.",
  "_rules": [
    "Keys are the 69 live tags in src/data/tags.json, and nothing else. Adding a key that isn't in the registry is how the taxonomy regrows junk.",
    "Matching is a plain case-insensitive substring count (see extractTags in scripts/sync-vlogs.js) — there are no word boundaries. A keyword that is a substring of a common word is a false positive on every video: 'orc' matches 'force', 'ork' matches 'work', 'rust' matches 'trust', 'event' matches 'eventually', 'tip' matches 'multiple', 'face' matches 'surface', 'iron' matches 'environment', 'cast' matches 'podcast', 'ice' matches 'nice'. Prefer the plural, a two-word phrase, or a proper noun.",
    "Scores are raw match counts and only the top 7 tags survive, so a long list of rare proper nouns is safe but a short list of chatty words is not.",
    "Retired tags live on as 301s in public/_redirects. When a tag is retired, fold its still-useful keywords into the tag it redirects to rather than deleting them."
  ],
